1
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:09,600
A few months ago,

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,400
the Veritas was translated again.

3
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:14,320
Everyone who worked on the translation

4
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,560
and everyone who subsequently read it

5
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:17,760
is now dead.

6
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:19,720
Your tutor's a what?

7
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,240
An alien.

8
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:23,040
What do you mean, an alien?

9
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,520
A space one.

10
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,840
A space alien.

11
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,000
Will you read the Veritas?

12
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,200
So, you're blind, and you don't want your enemies to know.

13
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:39,040
So your tutor ran a computer simulation?

14
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:42,520
Well, more like he got trapped inside one.

15
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,840
- Can that happen? - Yeah, he's a alien.

16
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:46,320
A space one.

17
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,760
Yeah, a space one.

18
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:52,600
Well, let's just call it a sort of dream.

19
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:02,760
Are you just completely mad?

20
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:05,080
- Is it working? - A little bit.

21
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:07,400
Not so mad then.

22
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,080
What are you doing?

23
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:13,440
I'm doing what everybody does when the world is in danger.

24
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:14,880
I'm calling the Doctor.

25
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:16,160
Pressing send.

26
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:22,040
So this computer simulation dream thing...

27
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:23,320
Yeah?

28
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,080
Which, to be clear, I don't believe a word of.

29
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,880
- Fair enough. - You said I was in it.

30
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:27,960
Yeah.

31
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:30,600
Well, how did it go? The dream version?

32
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:39,120
The Pope?

33
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,200
- In person. - The Pope

34
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:43,120
- in your flat here. - Yeah.

35
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:46,280
- Your tutor has strange dreams. - I bet he does, you know.

36
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:49,360
Maybe he's just trying to keep you on the straight and narrow.

37
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:52,400
Maybe, yeah.

38
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:56,360
How do you feel on the subject?

39
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:58,600
Whoa!

40
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,120
Stay where you are!

41
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,880
- Clear! - Please remain still and calm.

42
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,400
- Sit down. - Mmm-hmm.

43
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,640
Keep your hands in sight on the table.

44
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:10,240
- Miss Potts? - Yea h?

45
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:11,440
Who is this?

46
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:13,720
This is my friend Penny. Who the hell are you?

47
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,720
Room is secure, Your Excellency!

48
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,680
- This is Miss Potts, sir. - Hi.

49
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:24,360
Miss Potts, this is the Secretary-General of the UN.

50
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:27,880
I have flown here today to speak to the President.

51
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,480
I'm told you might be able to help.

52
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:33,200
I don't know the President.

53
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,280
How would I know the President? I mean,

54
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:38,240
I wouldn't have even voted for him. He's orange.

55
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:40,040
I mean, "the" President.

56
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:41,680
The Doctor.

57
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,480
The Doctor's not a president.

58
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:46,080
What's he president of?

59
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:47,720
Well...

60
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,600
In times of crisis,

61
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,280
Earth.

62
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:56,120
Is it okay if I get a move on?

63
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:00,480
President of the world?

64
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,360
In times of unusual danger,

65
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,760
that status is made official.

66
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:09,360
Turmezistan, near the border.

67
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,520
This is a disputed area.

68
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,240
A potential hot spot. The Chinese have troops here.

69
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:18,040
The Russians here.

70
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,560
The Americans here.

71
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,880
And in the centre...

72
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:23,080
A pyramid.

73
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:25,200
Sir? I have Colonel Brabbit on the line.

74
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:28,160
Colonel Brabbit, you're on with the Secretary-General.

75
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,800
Colonel, what have you to report?

76
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:32,920
Nothing, sir. Nothing at all.

77
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:35,120
It seems dormant.

78
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:38,280
The Russians and the Chinese are reporting the same.

79
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:40,720
Reporting what? What's dormant?

80
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:44,280
The pyramid. We're keeping it under observation.

81
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:47,760
Why? What's it been doing?

82
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,400
- You haven't told her? - I haven't, no.

83
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,480
It's a 5, 000-year-old pyramid.

84
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:54,120
There's one problem with that.

85
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,040
One little problem.

86
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,840
Wasn't there yesterday.

87
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,560
The end of your life

88
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:54,960
has already begun.

89
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,720
There's a last place

90
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,240
you will ever go.

91
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,520
A last store you will ever walk through.

92
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,080
A last sight you will ever see.

93
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:10,520
And every step you ever take

94
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:13,120
is moving you closer.

95
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:18,080
The end of the world...

96
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:22,200
Is a billion, billion tiny moments.

97
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:25,040
Don't shut the door!

98
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:27,480
And somewhere,

99
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:29,080
unnoticed... Sorry.

100
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,720
In silence or in darkness...

101
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:35,160
- Damn it. - It has already begun.

102
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:38,640
Are you talking to yourself in there?

103
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,240
I'm meditating.

104
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,400
Been in there for hours.

105
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,760
I've been trying to talk to you.

106
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:48,760
Have you double locked this thing?

107
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:52,040
I'm busy thinking.

108
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,960
Excellent. Who needs eyesight?

109
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:58,240
Those monk creatures I told you about.

110
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:01,600
If they've modelled every event in human history,

111
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:03,840
if they've simulated

112
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:06,720
entire events streamed from day one till now,

113
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:09,600
think what they'd know.

114
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,720
Think what they could do with that.

115
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:15,720
The UN called.

116
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,840
They want you in Turmezistan immediately.

117
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:19,160
Tell them no!

118
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,240
Oh.

119
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:25,320
They wouldn't take no for an answer.

120
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:29,880
How did they get it out of my office?

121
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,320
The windows aren't big enough.

122
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:34,400
Oh, er, they are now.

123
00:06:34,840 --> 00:06:36,440
Are you gonna ask what's going on?

124
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:39,240
Last I heard, you were on a date with Penny. What happened?

125
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:42,200
Uh, the, uh, United Nations Secretary-General.

126
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:44,680
- Awesome. - Nah, that wasn't a metaphor.

127
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:47,040
Good, because I really wasn't following it.

128
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,600
Mr President.

129
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,240
I'm very pleased to see you.

130
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:53,120
I think we have something of interest.

131
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:58,280
Why don't you tell me in your own words?

132
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,720
It's a matter of a pyramid.

133
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:06,960
Hello.

134
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,560
Hi.

135
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:22,920
Oh! You're an angel.

136
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:33,680
You look... Don't take this the wrong way.

137
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,160
You look awful.

138
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:37,720
How could anyone possibly take that the wrong way?

139
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,200
Big night last night?

140
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:43,080
There was drinking.

141
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,360
There were breakages.

142
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:46,640
Textbook.

143
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,640
We're going to stage two today.

144
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:50,360
Well, it'd be rude not to.

145
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,720
You okay mixing it?

146
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:53,120
I broke my reading glasses.

147
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,480
Tell me what you see.

148
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:11,000
It's a 5,000-year-old pyramid.

149
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:13,280
What do you know?

150
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:14,960
It wasn't there yesterday.

151
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:16,160
Therefore?

152
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:19,840
It's not really a pyramid.

153
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:22,640
It's something disguised as a pyramid that

154
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,600
just appeared out of thin air.

155
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:27,040
And that's all way beyond human technology

156
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:29,320
so it's gotta be alien. It's an alien spaceship.

157
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:30,760
There you go.

158
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,080
And what's it doing?

159
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:35,040
It could've chosen anywhere on this planet. It chose to sit

160
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:39,040
on the strategic intersection of the three most powerful armies on Earth.

161
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:41,000
So what it's doing, Colonel,

162
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:44,760
- is sending us a message. - What message?

163
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,480
Bring it.

164
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:57,320
- Mr President... - Sir? What are you doing?

165
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:01,800
Bringing it.

166
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,160
Nardole.

167
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,520
On it, sir.

168
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:08,880
What's he doing?

169
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:11,880
We don't know what the thing is capable of.

170
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,280
Nothing yet.

171
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:21,840
All looks fine.

172
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:24,080
What are you doing?

173
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,440
Oh, updating him.

174
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,320
There's something happening, sir.

175
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:49,040
It's opening up, sir.

176
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:50,800
There's a door.

177
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,320
Nardole?

178
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,720
Something's coming out, sir.

179
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:03,760
Going by the description you gave me from the simulation, sir,

180
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:06,120
I think that's one of the monk creatures.

181
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,480
Hello?

182
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:09,440
We know you.

183
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:12,040
Then you'll know that there is a line in the sand.

184
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:14,560
And I'm the man on the other side of it.

185
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:16,240
You wanna keep me that way.

186
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:19,600
We will take this planet and its people.

187
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:21,920
You will be prevented. You will be fought.

188
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,960
We will be invited.

189
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:29,000
We will take this world. We will rule its people.

190
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:32,080
But only when we're asked.

191
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,920
- We will talk again. - When?

192
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:38,560
At the end of the Earth.

193
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:53,400
- 11:57... - P.M.

194
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:55,080
Yeah, mine too.

195
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,560
It's everyone's.

196
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:01,480
11:57 p.m.

197
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:04,520
Did you get that, sir?

198
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:06,880
Everyone's phones gone to 11:57.

199
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,560
Yup. Same here.

200
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:09,920
What's...

201
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:12,720
What does that mean, 11:57?

202
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:15,960
Also known as, three minutes to midnight.

203
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:17,600
The Doomsday Clock.

204
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:20,280
- The what? - Symbolic clock face.

205
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:23,840
Representing a countdown to possible global catastrophes

206
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:26,920
started by some atomic scientists in 1947.

207
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:29,160
The closer they set the clock to midnight,

208
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:32,040
the closer we are to global disaster.

209
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,120
Currently it's set

210
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:35,840
at three minutes to midnight.

211
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:40,000
So now, every clock in the world is the Doomsday Clock.

212
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:42,720
- Thanks to the Monks, yes. - Is this a threat?

213
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,480
I wish it was. Did I tell you?

214
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:47,040
See, I think this is a warning.

215
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:50,240
Somewhere, somehow,

216
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:52,480
the end has begun.

217
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,040
Fully automated.

218
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,160
Lunch?

219
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,240
Well, it'd be rude not to.

220
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:50,520
- Hello. Privet. - Ah?

221
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:54,040
Sorry about that. Needed the call to zero in on your coordinates.

222
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:58,240
Now, this is the Secretary-General of the UN.

223
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:00,960
I am the President of the world.

224
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,960
And this is Xiaglian.

225
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,680
She's in charge of the Chinese Army.

226
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:09,040
Say hi to each other.

227
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:12,920
Now, we've been having a bit of a chat.

228
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:15,160
Thing is, World War Three.

229
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:18,040
What do you think? Basically, we're against it.

230
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:21,440
Listen to me.

231
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:24,320
Those creatures in that pyramid, they have studied your species,

232
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,400
your civilisation.

233
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:27,000
Your entire history.

234
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:28,600
They've run a computer simulation of this world

235
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:31,520
since you lot first slopped out of the ocean looking for a fight,

236
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:36,040
and they have chosen this exact moment and this exact place to arrive.

237
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:37,200
Why?

238
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:39,720
Because a war is about to break out.

239
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:41,200
Possibly.

240
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:43,760
But whatever it is,

241
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:46,680
they're right here, right now,

242
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,360
because they believe humanity

243
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,120
will be at its weakest.

244
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:53,640
Then we'll demonstrate strength.

245
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,480
We will attack the pyramid.

246
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:57,560
Force is never the answer.

247
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,320
Isn't that right, Doctor?

248
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:04,320
Contact your masters. Coordinate your attacks.

249
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:05,960
Doctor?

250
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,360
I doubt you'll even scratch that thing.

251
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,480
But if you demonstrate strength and unity,

252
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:12,520
they might choose to step away. Bill, take that look off your face.

253
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:14,560
There's no look on my face.

254
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:17,120
They did not come here in peace. We have to do what we can.

255
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:19,000
Yeah, I get it.

256
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:28,880
It's two minutes to now.

257
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:31,160
The Doomsday Clock is moving.

258
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:32,520
What do we do?

259
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:34,480
Coordinate your attacks.

260
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:48,880
What's wrong with him?

261
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:52,000
What's wrong with the Doctor?

262
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:12,400
Did Nardole send you to speak with me?

263
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:14,160
Mighta done.

264
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:16,640
Mighta said there was something you want to tell me.

265
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:21,000
Funny thing, fear, isn't it?

266
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,320
Once it rules you,

267
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,760
you're even afraid to admit what's scaring you.

268
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:33,960
For the record, I for one, fully understand my weakness.

269
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:38,160
Oh, God, what's that?

270
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:59,360
Approaching target. Permission to strike.

271
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:02,680
So, why's the pyramid active now?

272
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:04,880
Possibly they know they're about to be bombed.

273
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,720
Target distance 10 miles. Set position five degrees.

274
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:32,520
Code 12. Mayday. Mayday!

275
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:06,760
It's the Monks. They've hijacked the plane.

276
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,760
How did they do that?

277
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:26,120
Oh, they're fine. The crew are alive.

278
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,320
Who are those guys?

279
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,320
I think they're ours.

280
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:34,960
- Yours? - We targeted the pyramid with a missile.

281
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:46,800
From a submarine.

282
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,480
So demonstrating strength isn't going to help.

283
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:56,320
We are ready to talk.

284
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:07,600
Why don't you just take the afternoon off if you feel that bad?

285
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:11,720
I can't just take the afternoon off.

286
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,920
How 'bout a kip on the floor under your desk.

287
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,560
Now that's an idea I can get behind.

288
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:57,280
I mean, this is a trap. Right?

289
00:19:58,560 --> 00:19:59,640
Possibly.

290
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:01,680
Probably.

291
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:05,920
And we're just walking into it?

292
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:09,320
Well, every trap you walk into is a chance to learn about your enemies.

293
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,320
Impossible to set a trap

294
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:13,920
without making a self-portrait of your own weaknesses.

295
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:16,160
Great.

296
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:17,600
Unless it kills us.

297
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,680
Well, you could say that about anything.

298
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:46,280
The human race is about to end.

299
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:49,400
The chain of events is already in motion.

300
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:54,640
Life on Earth will cease by humanity's own hand.

301
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:57,000
Observe.

302
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:17,920
Ah.

303
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:20,560
The simulation machine looks a bit different from the outside.

304
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:23,080
We are modelling the future.

305
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:27,760
Each thread is a chain of days leading to your end.

306
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:31,560
We can detect when a catastrophe is about to occur.

307
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,600
- And? - Stop it from occurring.

308
00:21:34,840 --> 00:21:36,680
You don't look much like guardian angels.

309
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:40,160
We have chosen this form to look like you.

310
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:41,560
You look like corpses.

311
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:44,680
You are corpses to us.

312
00:21:45,440 --> 00:21:47,160
Your world is ending.

313
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,920
You can do nothing.

314
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,600
But we can save you.

315
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:51,880
Save us, then.

316
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:55,200
To save you, we must be asked.

317
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:56,720
Then what?

318
00:21:56,880 --> 00:21:59,080
We will protect you.

319
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:01,760
- How long for? - Forever.

320
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:05,840
Do you understand now?

321
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:08,040
Do you see?

322
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:11,960
Asking them for help has conditions.

323
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:15,000
Invite them in

324
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:18,520
and it will be the last free action you take.

325
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:23,240
If you do not ask for help then see the days to come.

326
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:30,880
These are the threads that lead to one year in your future.

327
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:34,320
Take them as proof.

328
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,400
What was that?

329
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:56,880
Planet Earth. Not a single living thing.

330
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:59,120
Dead as the moon.

331
00:22:59,760 --> 00:23:01,440
You seem pretty damn calm about it.

332
00:23:02,080 --> 00:23:04,000
Do I? Oh, I'm sorry.

333
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:06,880
It's not my first dead planet.

334
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:10,240
Ask for help. It will be given.

335
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:13,600
- Why do you need to be asked? - Power must consent.

336
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:15,400
"Power must consent." What does that mean?

337
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:18,120
Those who hold power in this world

338
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:21,400
must consent to our dominion.

339
00:23:22,760 --> 00:23:23,800
Why?

340
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:30,680
One minute to midnight.

341
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:34,880
You could take this planet in a... In a heartbeat.

342
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:37,280
Why do you need consent?

343
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:39,120
We must be wanted.

344
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:41,320
We must be loved.

345
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:44,960
- To rule through fear is inefficient. - Of course.

346
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:47,240
Fear is temporary. Love

347
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:49,560
is slavery.

348
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:53,040
If consent is what you need,

349
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:55,080
I consent now.

350
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:56,680
No. No.

351
00:23:56,760 --> 00:23:58,440
Don't do this, please. Don't even consider this...

352
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:00,320
What I saw is real.

353
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:02,840
I felt it.

354
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:08,120
If you can help us,

355
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:11,160
- I consent. - Please.

356
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,960
Listen to me.

357
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:19,040
Do you have power?

358
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:20,960
I have power.

359
00:24:21,040 --> 00:24:23,200
Does power consent?

360
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,960
Please, stop. just stop this!

361
00:24:26,040 --> 00:24:28,520
If your consent is impure,

362
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:30,560
it will kill you.

363
00:24:31,120 --> 00:24:32,840
Impure? What does that mean, impure?

364
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:34,760
You act out of fear.

365
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:37,120
Fear is not consent.

366
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,120
Planet Earth does not consent to your help,

367
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:52,480
your presence, or your conquest.

368
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:54,640
Thank you for playing the big pyramid game.

369
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:56,840
Bye-bye. See you again next week. Hopefully not.

370
00:24:56,920 --> 00:24:59,960
Without our help, planet Earth is doomed.

371
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:02,800
Yes. Well, it's been doomed before.

372
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:06,000
Guess what happened? Me.

373
00:25:20,120 --> 00:25:22,400
- What are you doing? - I just need a minute.

374
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:24,560
I was about to throw up in my suit.

375
00:25:24,800 --> 00:25:25,840
I did that once.

376
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:26,920
Urgh.

377
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:38,280
Oh, my God.

378
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:46,920
Okay. Whatever that is, that is not meant to happen.

379
00:25:49,040 --> 00:25:50,800
We need to sort this.

380
00:26:11,280 --> 00:26:13,200
Why do they need consent?

381
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:14,960
Maybe they're like vampires.

382
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:16,880
Can't come in unless they're invited.

383
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:18,320
They're not vampires.

384
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:20,760
The future we saw, is it the war?

385
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:22,960
Do we bring the future?

386
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:25,640
That would seem to be the most obvious conclusion.

387
00:26:25,680 --> 00:26:28,200
No! I say no. Friend?

388
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:30,120
I will not fight you.

389
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:31,680
We are just soldiers in the field.

390
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:33,560
Are we too afraid to disobey?

391
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:35,600
I'm not.

392
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:42,720
Neither am I.

393
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:45,800
This is amazing.

394
00:26:46,400 --> 00:26:48,480
What do you think, Mr President?

395
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:51,800
Did we just... Give peace a chance?

396
00:26:55,360 --> 00:26:57,160
The clock.

397
00:26:58,280 --> 00:26:59,480
Sorry?

398
00:27:00,120 --> 00:27:02,520
Look at the clock.

399
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:04,760
Still one minute to midnight.

400
00:27:05,640 --> 00:27:07,440
It made no difference.

401
00:27:07,520 --> 00:27:09,160
How could this make no difference?

402
00:27:09,240 --> 00:27:11,720
Because it's not you who's going to end the world.

403
00:27:12,480 --> 00:27:13,680
You were never the problem.

404
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:15,080
Then who is the problem?

405
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:17,480
Something is happening somewhere else.

406
00:27:18,280 --> 00:27:20,200
Somewhere in the world.

407
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:22,360
In silence or in darkness.

408
00:27:22,920 --> 00:27:24,880
The world is ending, right now.

409
00:27:25,520 --> 00:27:27,320
And we have to find out where.

410
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:32,200
It's gone crazy.

411
00:27:32,800 --> 00:27:34,160
It's much too strong.

412
00:27:34,200 --> 00:27:36,240
It's not just breaking the root system down,

413
00:27:36,320 --> 00:27:37,680
it's killing the whole thing.

414
00:27:38,520 --> 00:27:39,800
We have to seal off the lab.

415
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:41,640
The greenhouse. Everything.

416
00:27:41,720 --> 00:27:43,760
This can't be allowed to get into the atmosphere.

417
00:27:50,320 --> 00:27:53,680
This is impossible. We can't search a whole planet in a few minutes.

418
00:27:53,760 --> 00:27:57,200
Narrow it down. They landed the pyramid in the middle of a military crisis.

419
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:59,080
What was the point of that?

420
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:01,400
Okay, what was the point?

421
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:05,200
What was the effect? They told us the world was ending

422
00:28:05,280 --> 00:28:07,160
in a potential war zone.

423
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:09,000
What did we assume was going to happen?

424
00:28:09,080 --> 00:28:10,120
World War Three.

425
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:12,360
But it didn't. The trick with misdirection,

426
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:15,680
don't look where the arrow is pointing. Look where it's pointing away from.

427
00:28:15,760 --> 00:28:21,080
So, what's already on our radar that we should be worried about, right now?

428
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:24,280
Forgot about war. What else could end the world?

429
00:28:24,360 --> 00:28:27,080
- Bacteria. - I like the sound of that.

430
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:29,880
New strain of flu? Plague?

431
00:28:30,320 --> 00:28:32,280
People can be immune. And whatever it is,

432
00:28:32,360 --> 00:28:35,280
it will kill all life on Earth. Not just humans.

433
00:28:35,800 --> 00:28:37,960
Plague discriminates.

434
00:28:38,040 --> 00:28:40,600
So this isn't a plan. It's a mistake.

435
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:43,840
Somebody, somewhere, is doing something

436
00:28:43,920 --> 00:28:46,080
that's about to blow up in everybody's face.

437
00:28:55,720 --> 00:28:57,000
What are you doing?

438
00:28:57,080 --> 00:28:59,840
A distraction tells that whatever's coming

439
00:28:59,920 --> 00:29:02,720
is already on a watch list.

440
00:29:03,840 --> 00:29:06,680
I just put all the top secret intelligence documents in the world

441
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:08,640
online, in searchable format!

442
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:11,000
- What? - Sit down and google!

443
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:20,760
It's never done anything like that before.

444
00:29:21,400 --> 00:29:22,880
Check the mix.

445
00:29:24,920 --> 00:29:26,000
Anything?

446
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:29,320
Douglas?

447
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,080
Douglas!

448
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:33,680
Douglas!

449
00:29:54,440 --> 00:29:56,440
- Doctor, listen. - What?

450
00:29:56,520 --> 00:29:58,720
Isn't it worth at least just considering doing the deal?

451
00:29:58,760 --> 00:30:01,040
- What deal? - All we have to do is consent.

452
00:30:01,120 --> 00:30:03,720
That's what the Secretary-General thought, and they burned him.

453
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:07,200
He was afraid. I'm not being afraid, I'm being smart.

454
00:30:07,280 --> 00:30:10,280
Yeah. Being smart is not giving away your planet.

455
00:30:10,800 --> 00:30:14,280
So, an accident leading to irrevocable consequences.

456
00:30:14,320 --> 00:30:15,640
I like bacteria.

457
00:30:16,120 --> 00:30:19,400
They can spread. Once they're out, you can't put them away again.

458
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:21,720
What could they do? What do you depend on?

459
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:23,960
Air, water, food, beer.

460
00:30:24,080 --> 00:30:27,400
Air, water, and food. Let's say something's going to change,

461
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:30,600
something is going to be released. Something

462
00:30:31,360 --> 00:30:33,720
new, something fast, I'm feeling...

463
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:36,800
I'm feeling biochemical.

464
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:39,120
- Check biochemical trials. - Yes, sir.

465
00:30:39,520 --> 00:30:40,880
Doctor.

466
00:30:41,920 --> 00:30:45,120
That world was dead a year from now.

467
00:30:45,600 --> 00:30:47,000
We should at least go in there and talk.

468
00:30:47,080 --> 00:30:51,520
Well, there are about a hundred thousand biochemical trials going on right now.

469
00:30:51,600 --> 00:30:54,200
Specifically related to GM bacteria.

470
00:30:54,240 --> 00:30:55,880
Uh, 6,000?

471
00:30:57,040 --> 00:30:59,600
How many have reached stage two? You cannot accept their offer.

472
00:30:59,880 --> 00:31:01,400
Why not?

473
00:31:01,480 --> 00:31:03,360
Because whatever the price is, it's too high.

474
00:31:03,440 --> 00:31:04,440
We'll work it out.

475
00:31:04,520 --> 00:31:05,920
428.

476
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:08,480
It's too many. And we don't even know if you're right.

477
00:31:08,560 --> 00:31:10,000
Well, I probably am.

478
00:31:10,040 --> 00:31:11,360
"Probably" isn't good enough.

479
00:31:11,440 --> 00:31:12,960
Well, "probably" is all you have got!

480
00:31:13,040 --> 00:31:15,040
It's your planet, I can't just give it away.

481
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:19,120
You know what, sir? Finally you've said something I agree with.

482
00:31:19,840 --> 00:31:21,440
It's our planet.

483
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:23,000
Our choice.

484
00:31:23,080 --> 00:31:24,120
You can't make a deal with them.

485
00:31:24,200 --> 00:31:26,000
You don't know what you're agreeing to. I don't know.

486
00:31:26,080 --> 00:31:29,960
All I know is, I plan on living to fight another day.

487
00:31:30,880 --> 00:31:34,440
Right now, what we don't have is a whole lot of other days.

488
00:31:34,520 --> 00:31:36,680
- Ag reed. - Also agreed.

489
00:31:37,880 --> 00:31:39,240
Doctor.

490
00:31:42,120 --> 00:31:44,800
Is it just possible that they're right?

491
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:48,280
Being right is easy. We need to win.

492
00:31:49,720 --> 00:31:52,480
All these soldiers in the room, and you're the only one still fighting.

493
00:31:52,960 --> 00:31:54,360
Would you make the deal?

494
00:31:54,440 --> 00:31:55,960
Even not knowing what's going to happen?

495
00:31:56,040 --> 00:32:00,560
Those guys have modelled every event in human history, to find our weak spot.

496
00:32:00,920 --> 00:32:02,920
Are you gonna do the same in a couple of minutes?

497
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:05,200
- Would you make the deal? - No.

498
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:07,280
Not if I had a choice.

499
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:09,560
But we don't. Do we?

500
00:32:09,600 --> 00:32:11,120
It's your world.

501
00:32:11,520 --> 00:32:13,080
Not any more.

502
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:16,480
Okay-

503
00:32:17,760 --> 00:32:20,760
Back to the pyramid. And negotiate our surrender.

504
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:28,160
Doctor.

505
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:30,440
What are you gonna do?

506
00:32:30,520 --> 00:32:32,240
Well, for a start, I'm going to tell you the truth.

507
00:32:32,760 --> 00:32:34,920
I've been keeping a secret from you.

508
00:32:41,360 --> 00:32:42,440
Doctor?

509
00:32:44,520 --> 00:32:47,760
We can blind them. That's how we do it.

510
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:50,200
We blind them.

511
00:32:50,280 --> 00:32:51,720
Blind who? The Monks?

512
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:54,360
Bill, go to the pyramid. Keep an eye on them all.

513
00:32:54,400 --> 00:32:57,200
- Nardole, with me, to the TARDIS! - Yes, sir.

514
00:32:57,280 --> 00:32:59,160
Have you got a plan?

515
00:32:59,640 --> 00:33:01,520
You'll be hearing from me.

516
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:04,960
Biohazard. Lab in lockdown.

517
00:33:06,120 --> 00:33:08,880
Biohazard. Lab in lockdown.

518
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:12,880
Biohazard. Lab in lockdown.

519
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:16,680
Biohazard. Lab in lockdown.

520
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:20,640
Oh, Douglas, what have you done?

521
00:33:21,160 --> 00:33:24,520
Okay, there's a list of labs on the unit watch list.

522
00:33:24,600 --> 00:33:28,360
If they're being watched, that means that they've got CCTV cameras

523
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:31,440
with feeds to Unit 8Q.

524
00:33:31,480 --> 00:33:34,360
- Can you hack them? - Course I can, I'm not just sexy.

525
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:37,280
But there's 428 of them, we can't watch them all.

526
00:33:37,320 --> 00:33:40,480
- Are you following me? - Yeah, I think I get it.

527
00:33:40,560 --> 00:33:42,160
Yes, well, we're not going to watch them,

528
00:33:42,200 --> 00:33:43,200
we're going to switch them off,

529
00:33:43,320 --> 00:33:46,240
- can you do that? - What good would switching them off do?

530
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:50,720
If I'm right, the Monks are only watching one of those labs.

531
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:52,280
How would they do that?

532
00:33:52,360 --> 00:33:55,480
Well, I suppose they'd just... Hack the cameras!

533
00:33:56,040 --> 00:33:57,440
So switch 'em off.

534
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:06,040
Okay, so... We've blinded them.

535
00:34:06,480 --> 00:34:08,520
But whatever's happening is still happening.

536
00:34:08,680 --> 00:34:10,680
- Yup. - And the Monks are powerful.

537
00:34:10,720 --> 00:34:13,160
They can just turn the cameras back on.

538
00:34:13,240 --> 00:34:14,480
Yes, they can.

539
00:34:14,560 --> 00:34:16,400
But they're only watching one lab.

540
00:34:17,040 --> 00:34:21,280
So all we need to know is which lab just got its cameras back?

541
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:26,600
Oh, you genius.

542
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:28,920
Boom.

543
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:38,960
Oh, my God.

544
00:34:39,080 --> 00:34:40,600
No, I'm the Doctor.

545
00:34:40,680 --> 00:34:42,880
But it's an easy mistake to make. The eyebrows.

546
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:44,840
